; Plan 03's exactness table, as a document: one note on every landmark
; the grid was CHOSEN to hold exactly.
;
;   TPQ           46 126 080   one quarter note
;   TPQ / 2       23 063 040   an eighth
;   TPQ / 3       15 375 360   a triplet eighth — the reason for the 3
;   TPQ / 4       11 531 520   a sixteenth
;   TPQ / 5        9 225 216   a quintuplet
;   TPQ / 7        6 589 440   a septuplet
;   PPC              720 720   one pacer tick (TPQ = 64 · PPC)
;   TPQ / 960         48 048   one SMF tick at division 960
;   TPQ / 480         96 096   …and at 480
;   IT tick        1 921 920   TPQ / 24, IT's own tick at 24 per quarter
;
; Every one of them is an integer, which is the whole claim. The dump
; below is where the printer says so back, by plan 03's rule: a tick with
; an exact short decimal in quarters reads as `Nq` — 720 720 is
; `0.015625q` and 9 225 216 is `0.2q` — and the rest read as `Nt`,
; because 1/3, 1/7 and 1/960 of a quarter have no such decimal.
(timeline :title "grid-table" :length 1bar)

(tempo-point :at 0q :us 500000)
(meter-point :at 0bar :sig [4 4])

(lane :name grid :kind notes :target grid
  (note :at 0q        :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 48048t    :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 96096t    :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 720720t   :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 1921920t  :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 6589440t  :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 9225216t  :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 0.25q     :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 15375360t :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 0.5q      :dur 1t :key 60)
  (note :at 1q        :dur 1t :key 60))
